From 283b0726637baa1bf7542e7905ac30191f6217e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <226450061+logdog2325@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 22:41:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 160/161] XD Netplay: netplay multi battles, phase 1 fixes
 (fill seats, route ping, quiet delay notice, GBA input)

- MultiFillSeats: a lone guest plays Seats 3 and 4 whichever seat the join
  order gave it (the claim only; lobby seats and the leave check keep the real
  holder), so a two-machine Multi room can start. With more guests an empty
  Seat 3 or 4 repeats the other.
- Multi route ping: a guest's measured 0 ms (LAN) counts as 1; only a guest
  whose first pong is still out makes the route unknown.
- A lobby whose pad map a Multi game left behind is sized by seat (host and
  Seat 3 after a switch back to 1v1), not by the old four-seat map.
- Edge-safe lower: sticks and triggers repeat within 2, so a jittery
  controller (Wii U adapter) still lets channel 0 give back entries.
- "Input delay is at its limit" mid-battle goes as an XdNotice (kind 5) that
  each client writes to the room chat only; the pre-boot copy is unchanged.
- Solo launches that are not a solo Multi take back port 4's GBA; Android
  keeps port 1 on XD Multi only with MultiEnabled on, and migrates only GBA
  ROM slots 2 and 3 into EMERALD.gba.
- Android GBA input: the port-1 GBA requests focus again (focus opens the
  input gate; SI port 1 is device 14, so no GC port is blocked). A GC pad
  this machine does not play in the running game no longer counts as sharing
  a GBA's controller, so a joiner's physical GBA buttons stay live after a
  top-screen tap, as in 1.7.5. The pad lookup clears on every stop and when
  the client is destroyed.
- Multi seats: the joiner's model pick is disabled ("Multi uses each save's
  own model."); the Watch only tooltip says a change applies after the host
  stops the game; quick match skips "[Multi] " rooms.
